oretical and practical input .\par }\pard\plain \s1\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel0\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\lang1031\kerning28\cgrid {\lang2057 \page \sect }\sectd \psz9\pgnrestart\linex0\endnhere\sectdefaultcl {\header \pard\plain \s28\qj\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\brsp20 \tqr\tx9072\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\f1\fs20 Basic Understanding\tab }{\field{\*\fldinst {\cs38\f1\fs20  PAGE }}{\fldrslt {\cs38\f1\fs20\lang1024 9}}}{\f1\fs20 \par }}\pard\plain \s1\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel0\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\lang1031\kerning28\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505000}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505082}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505149}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505317}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382719217}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828866}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896585}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011193}1. A Basic Conception of Voting and Rating{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505000}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505082}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505149}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505317}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382719217}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828866}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896585}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011193}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 \par This section  presents some basic considerations which should lead to  a clearer view of important elements in rating and voting processes. It tries to develop a conce}{\lang2057 p}{\lang2057 tion that integrates different forms of people\rquote s expression of preferences known by the terms \lquote rating\rquote  and \lquote voting\rquote . This open perspective is taken to enco}{\lang2057 m}{\lang2057 pass a variety of rating activities that should allow us to see - or rather make - linkages between everyday rating activities and rating in the context of co}{\lang2057 m}{\lang2057 puter-mediated communication.\par \par }\pard\plain \s2\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\i\f1\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505001}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505083}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505150}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505318}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382719218}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828867}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896586}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011194}1.1. Some Remarks on Definitions{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505001}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505083}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505150}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505318}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382719218}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828867}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896586}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011194}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 First, a definition of computer-mediated communication (CMC) must be given, as  this term will be used extensively throughout the study. A definition by John December may serve as a general reference :\par }\pard\plain \s15\li1134\ri1134\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 'Computer-mediated communication (CMC) is the process by which people create, e}{\lang2057 x}{\lang2057 change, and perceive information using networked telecommunications systems that facil}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 tate encoding, transmitting, and decoding messages.'\line  (http://www.december.com/john/study/cmc/what.html)\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 Developing a basic conception of voting and rating in the context of computer-mediated co}{\lang2057 m}{\lang2057 munication may start with looking at various definitions of voting and rating.  While the term \lquote voting\rquote  seems to be clearly understood as the act of expressing one's prefe}{\lang2057 r}{\lang2057 ences in a decision-making process, there appear to be different uses of the term \lquote rating\rquote .  The following is a definition of rating which comes from computer-mediated communication. Rating is defined as\par }\pard\plain \s15\qj\li1134\ri1134\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 '(a) process by which someone reviews a document on the Internet and applies a subjective value.' (Net Shepherd 1996; 26)\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 In contrast to this action-oriented definition, another one taken from a social sciences dictionary describes  a rating as \par }\pard\plain \s15\qj\li1134\ri1134\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 'a number indicating an evaluation of something along some given dimension.' (McC.Miller & Wilson 1983; 92)\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 These two different meanings of \lquote rating\rquote  can be found in many uses of the word. Taking into account both of them leads to the conclusion that the term \lquote rating\rquote  may be considered as the action and also as the outcome of any evaluation of an object.\par \par In this report both meanings of \lquote rating\rquote  are used. They are connected in the following way: Our basic conception starts from the individual.\par Any individual who assigns a value to an object is \lquote rating\rquote . Through this action the object receives a value which is also called a \lquote rating\rquote . Using  the term \lquote rating\rquote  we therefore have to consider two meanings: \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1. \tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls5\pnrnot0\pndec\pnb0\pni0\pnfs24\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxta . }}\ls5\adjustright {\lang2057 \lquote rating\rquote  as a verb, which denotes an action, and\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2. \tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls5\pnrnot0\pndec\pnb0\pni0\pnfs24\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxta . }}\ls5\adjustright {\lang2057 \lquote rating\rquote  as the outcome/result of this action.\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\lang2057 \par Individual ratings of an object may be collected and put together. Thus one may find out the average rating of an object in a certain population. Such a procedure results in a collective rating. Individual ratings of different objects may be compared. Thus one may find out which one of two or more objects are  rated highest. Such a procedure is usually called a \lquote vote\rquote .\par \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505002}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505084}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011195}Similarities between Voting and Rating{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505002}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505084}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011195}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 It is assumed in this report that on a certain  level of abstraction a common basis of voting and rating can be found. Rating is the most general term which denotes the evaluation of an object under scrutiny.  Such an evaluation can take place in terms of agreement or disagreement, approval or disa}{\lang2057 p}{\lang2057 proval, like or dislike, as well as in terms of relevance according to a chosen point of reference (e.g. quality, appropriateness, special interest).\par \par It is suggested to define  voting as a specific form of rating, i.e. voting means that a rating of one (or more) given object(s) is staged at a specific time under specific cond}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 tions.\par \par It is important to note that the distinction between rating and voting, or rather the subo}{\lang2057 r}{\lang2057 dination of voting to rating, is made at the level of social action. One may  see similarities of social action which probably do not appear if one only looks at how ratings or votes are processed (with or without the use of computers).}{\cs37\lang2057\super \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s25\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang2057\cgrid {\cs37\super \chftn }{ These remarks reflect a discussion on terminology in which Jacob Palme expressed some reservations against this view of rating on a rather abstract level.}}}{\lang2057 \par It seems necessary to be aware of both perspectives - agency vs. procedure - because each of them highlights an important aspect of rating:\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (1)\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-454\li454\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls6\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent454\pnsp170\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\ls6\adjustright {\lang2057 Dealing with rating and voting as related forms of social action one gains an insight into the essentially \ldblquote rated\rdblquote  nature of many everyday activities.\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (2)\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-454\li454\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls6\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent454\pnsp170\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\ls6\adjustright {\lang2057 -Looking at the different procedures of rating and voting points to relevant shortcomings of traditional methods which may be overcome through the use of computer-mediated commun}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 cation.\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\lang2057 \par To illustrate the variety of possible rating activities, including voting, one may imagine a co}{\lang2057 n}{\lang2057 tinuum of conditions.\par \par }\trowd \trqc\trgaph71\trleft-71 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx6733\pard \qj\widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057   fixed    }{\lang2057 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 35 \\f "Lucida Bright Math Symbol" \\s 12}{\fldrslt\f20\fs24}}{\field{\*\fldinst S