tings\cell }\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 \row }\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 certain time\cell }\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\tx496\adjustright {\lang2057 any time\cell }\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 \row }\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 certain topic,\cell }\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\tx496\adjustright {\lang2057 any object,\cell }\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 \row }\trowd \trqc\trgaph71\trleft-71 \clvertalt\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx3331\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx6733\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 etc.\cell }\pard \qc\widctlpar\intbl\tx496\adjustright {\lang2057 etc.\cell }\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright {\lang2057 \row }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\lang2057 \par In many cases of voting the conditions are fixed, i.e. the population, the agenda, the time and the voting model are defined, but there are also settings imaginable where a vote is conducted under fewer restrictions.\par \par The following considerations dealing with rating on a general level always imply the case of voting, too. Our conception can be summarised as follows:\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-284\li284\sb120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls7\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxta .}}\ls7\adjustright {\lang2057 We regard }{\i\lang2057 rating}{\lang2057  as a form of social action in which an individual assigns a value to an object a}{\lang2057 c}{\lang2057 cording to his or her knowledge, interests, or opinions.\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-284\li284\sb120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls8\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxta .}}\ls8\adjustright {\lang2057 We regard }{\i\lang2057 ratings}{\lang2057 , which are the aggregated outcomes of rating processes, on the one hand as an aid in decision-making and, on the other hand, as context enhancement in computer-mediated communication. Ratings may indicate individual and/or collective pre}{\lang2057 f}{\lang2057 erences. They can be used to solve a decision problem or to provide people with additional information for orientation in some knowledge space or social space.\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f0\lang2057 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-284\li284\sb120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls9\pnrnot0\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxta .}}\ls9\adjustright {\lang2057 We regard }{\i\lang2057 voting}{\lang2057  as a form of rating under specific conditions. Roughly sketched, these conditions incorporate the following restrictions: a given agenda, a fixed  time, closed participation. In contrast to rating procedures, the restrictions are necessary elements of voting procedures in order to ensure a legitimate output.\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\lang2057 \par }\pard\plain \s2\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\i\f1\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505003}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505085}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505151}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505319}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382719219}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828868}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896587}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011196}1.2. Outcomes of Voting and Rating Processes{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505003}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505085}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505151}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505319}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382719219}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828868}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896587}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011196}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 In addition to the individual action of voting or rating one has to think of the collective ou}{\lang2057 t}{\lang2057 come of voting or rating processes. These results  seem to be most relevant with respect to decision-making and information filtering.\par \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505004}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505086}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011197}Information Filtering{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505004}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505086}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011197}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 People have always developed filters to extract information which is of specific interest and value for them (e.g. following opinion leaders, orientation after  friends). At present,  the techn}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 cal means of filtering which use ratings in different ways are becoming more and more prom}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 nent. Due to the mass of content on the Internet, the filtering of information is currently a big issue.  Information filtering is a task of solving two converging problems (see Resnik et al. 1994):\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 finding information which is desirable (filtering in)\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 eliminating information which is undesirable (filtering out).\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 \par These two corresponding aspects of information filtering have prompted research on the best strategies for a long time. According to Malone et al. (1987; cited in Resnik et al. 1994) three categories of filtering techniques can be distinguished :\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 Cognitive: content-based\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 Social: collaborative, based on the subjective evaluations of others\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 Economic: based on the costs and benefits of producing and reading pieces of information.\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 \par Ratings can be the basis of mechanisms to filter information in each of the three ways. Ho}{\lang2057 w}{\lang2057 ever, nowadays in computer-mediated communication content-based and collaborative filtering of information are most common.\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 Content-based filtering finds its  main use in the need to restrict or block access to content which is deemed inappropriate for certain persons (e.g. children).\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\lang2057 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-283\li283\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls10\adjustright {\lang2057 Collaborative filtering covers a need of people who want to associate with similar minds.\par }\pard\plain \s15\li1134\ri1275\sb120\sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 'A collaborative system provides the means of accumulating the collective opinions of different people so that others can make use of the collective opinion for finding and filtering information.\rquote  (Net She}{\lang2057 p}{\lang2057 herd 1996; 6)\par }\pard \s15\qj\li1134\ri1275\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 Collaborative filtering is a technique that we all use, probably every day, without realising it. Before we go see a movie, go to a new restaurant, or buy some new software, we talk to people. The people that we talk to are people that we trust, and with whom we have agreed in the past, we gather opinions, and then apply them to the current decision. \line  (GroupLens; http://www.cs.umn.edu/Research/GroupLens/web/collab-intro.html)\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 \par The outcomes of rating processes can supply both the content-based as well as the collabor}{\lang2057 a}{\lang2057 tive filtering techniques with answers to the question which information to choose and what to leave out.\par \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505005}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505087}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011198}Decision-making{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505005}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505087}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011198}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 The processes of voting and rating are both important elements of decision-making: \par }\pard \qj\fi-284\li284\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 - The outcome of }{\i\lang2057 rating}{\lang2057  processes provides people with information about the preferences or opinions of other people. Thus people may learn about their environment in terms of common attitudes and shared interests. This supports their ability to make decisions based on inform}{\lang2057 a}{\lang2057 tion about the distribution of approval and disapproval (in addition to information about the question itself which is decided). This additional information is relevant in individual as well as collective decision-making processes (e.g. buying a product or casting a vote). Correspondingly, market research and opinion polls investigate this kind of information, which is then distributed through the mass media. \par }\pard \qj\li284\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 \par }\pard \qj\fi-284\li284\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 - The outcome of }{\i\lang2057 voting}{\lang2057  processes is closer to actual decision-making. They represent the aggregated individual preferences on a specific subject. These results may be connected with consequences to a different degree: In a \lquote loose\rquote  connection, e.g. the election of representatives to a parliament, the outcome of a vote does not prescribe any immediate action. The elected candidates have won a seat, but their further actions are determined only vaguely. In a \lquote tight\rquote  connection, e.g. a referendum on a country becoming a member of the European Union, the outcome of a vote leads to a well-known consequence. When the voters decide for or against joining, there is not much scope for interpreting this decision in different ways.\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\lang2057 \par }\pard\plain \s2\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\i\f1\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505006}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505088}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505152}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505320}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382719220}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828869}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896588}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011199}1.3. A Sociological Model of Rating{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505006}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505088}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505152}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505320}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382719220}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828869}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896588}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011199}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 Starting from an institutional perspective, the basic elements of rating may be identified and will later be expressed in a procedural definition.  Ratings and rating activities seem to be a common or even necessary part of our life. There are several institutions whose functions  are centred  on the processing of ratings. }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\lang2057  REF _Ref381620586 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt {\lang2057 Table 111}}}{\lang2057  shows three of the institutions involved in rating processes which are assumed to be especially interesting as \lquote ideal types\rquote  in the context of computer-supported rating (see section 2 for more examples).One should note that those institutions may themselves undergo changes through the e}{\lang2057 m}{\lang2057 ployment of computer networks.\par \par }\pard\plain \s18\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Ref381620586}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828381}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896177}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011413}Table }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\lang2057  SEQ Table \\* ARABIC }}{\fldrslt {\lang1024 1}}}{\lang2057 {\*\bkmkend _Ref381620586}: Rating institutions{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828381}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896177}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011413}\par }\trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30 \trbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw30 \trbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw30 \trbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw30 \trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrv\brdrs\brdrw15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw30 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx3000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx6070\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw30 \cltxlrtb \cellx9140\pard\plain \qc\sb120\sa120\widctlpar