 forms by a }{\i\lang2057 ranking choice, }{\lang2057 an}{\i\lang2057  evaluation choice }{\lang2057 and an}{\i\lang2057  allocative choice}{\lang2057 .}{\cs37\lang2057\super \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s25\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang2057\cgrid {\cs37\super \chftn }{ Mclean (1989) states that \lquote (a) good procedure should record voters\rquote  full preference schedules\rquote  (53).}}}{\lang2057  But note that only with a ranking choice algorithms are established which may determine a winning option. If individual preferences are expressed by using evaluation or allocative choices one may only calculate st}{\lang2057 a}{\lang2057 tistics to facilitate inferring a winning option.}{\fs26\lang2057 \par }{\lang2057 \par In addition to the determination of a winner, the collective outcome of a vote may be presented in the form of frequency tables showing the number of preferences falling into each of several different categories. Also some statistics - like mean, median, etc. - may be calculated depen}{\lang2057 d}{\lang2057 ing on the scale.\par \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011255}Voting definition script{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011255}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 The following section  describes scripting elements used in  the configuration of  voting activities. Web4Groups  employs  a config-file like notation and does not specify the syntax in BNF, as some details may change in the implement}{\lang2057 a}{\lang2057 tion phase. The script is usually generated via a web interface, but it can also be edited by the voting organiser (e.g. to make small changes on request of other users) or it  can be su}{\lang2057 b}{\lang2057 mitted to a voting activity by its organiser via e-mail as MIME-Content-Type "text/Web4Groups-VoteScript" using the Web4Groups e-mail gateway.\par \par A voting activity may hold more than one questions to vote on. Each section starts with a "StartQuestion" tag (see }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\lang2057  REF _Ref382663071 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt {\lang2057 Figure 6666}}}{\lang2057  for the voting script syntax).\par \par In each voting model there will certainly be more features  to define. However, the general d}{\lang2057 e}{\lang2057 sign principle is: do not  make it too complicated for a user to set up a vote or to understand (and possibly edit) the vote script. For instance: whether a ranking is to be checked if it is unique should not be a matter of configuration, as the organiser of a vote will expect that the system provides such a check of a user's input. Also, most configuration entries have default values. So it is just a matter of a few lines to set up a simple voting activity. The result should always contain frequencies (absolute numbers, or percent) and may contain other statistical values, as applicable, depending on the "Statistics" tag.\par \par Default values (bold) are used if a line is omitted. The default values for Evaluation Choice is "preferred":"acceptable":"not acceptable", as this value set supports decision-making pro}{\lang2057 c}{\lang2057 esses in small groups best. Hi2Low and Low2Hi indicate the order of literal values, so that numer}{\lang2057 i}{\lang2057 cal values can be assigned for calculating means of each option. The assigned values should also be shown near each literal value in the input form. The literal value indicated as "low" starts with numerical value = 1; the stepsize is 1.\par \par The organiser of the voting activity may force a closing of the vote with a special command to the voting agent.\par \par }\pard\plain \s18\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Ref382663071}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382800932}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011353}Figure }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\lang2057  SEQ Figure \\* ARABIC }}{\fldrslt {\lang1024 6}}}{\lang2057 {\*\bkmkend _Ref382663071}: Voting script syntax{\*\bkmkend _Toc382800932}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011353}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\fs18\lang2057 StartQuestion\tab \tab \tab \tab // start tag for question\tab \par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\tx3969\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 The question text follows. It may contain line breaks.\par No HTML tags are allowed, as they would also be shown when sending the question via an e-mail gateway. \par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 EndQuestion\tab \tab \tab \tab // end tag for question\par }\pard \qj\fi-1134\li1134\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 VotingModel=}{\b\fs18\lang2057 BinaryChoice}{\fs18\lang2057  | \tab \tab // select one option out of 2\par \tab SingleSelectionChoice | \tab // select one option out of N\par \tab MultipleSelectionChoice | \tab // select one or more options\par \tab RankingChoice | \tab \tab // rank options from 1 to N\par \tab EvaluationChoice | \tab \tab // assign  values to options\par \tab AllocativeChoice\tab \tab // assign points to options from a given budget\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 Options="option1":...:"optionN"\tab //  e.g. BinaryChoice: "ok":"not ok", if not specified default is: }{\b\fs18\lang2057 "yes":"no"}{\fs18\lang2057  \par }\pard \qj\ri-284\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 \tab \tab \tab \tab // all other models e.g.: "Use a screwdriver", "Ask a committee",...,"Hire consultant"\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 Abstain=}{\b\fs18\lang2057 yes}{\fs18\lang2057  | no | default\tab \tab // add an additional choice: "abstain", can be made default checked\par }\pard \qj\ri-426\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 Values=\tab \tab \tab \tab // only needed as second dimension for EvaluationChoice\par \tab "value1":...:"valueM"\{:Low2Hi | Hi2Low\} |\tab // e.g. "best":"good":"poor":Hi2Low\par \tab start:end\{:step\} |\tab \tab //  e.g. 0:10:2; stepsize forces input form to make checkboxes at 0,2,4,6,8,10\par \tab budget\tab \tab \tab // for AllocativeChoice: specify vote budget, e.g. Values=100\par }\pard \qj\ri-1134\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 \tab \tab \tab \tab // if not specified default is: }{\b\fs18\lang2057 "preferred":"acceptable":"not acceptable":Hi2Low}{\fs18\lang2057 \par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 ChangeVote=}{\b\fs18\lang2057 yes}{\fs18\lang2057  | no\tab \tab // allow a user to change vote while voting is pending\par ShowResults=}{\b\fs18\lang2057 closed}{\fs18\lang2057  | open | all | K\tab // when to show results: only if K/all votes arrived\par AnonymousVote=yes | }{\b\fs18\lang2057 no}{\fs18\lang2057 \tab \tab \tab // individual voting result remains anonymous\par }\pard \qj\ri141\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 VoteOpens=}{\b\fs18\lang2057 now}{\fs18\lang2057  | yyyy:mm:dd-\{hh:mm}{\fs16\lang2057 \} | dd\tab // date or number of days from now}{\fs18\lang2057 \par }\pard \qj\ri-142\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 VoteCloses=yyyy:mm:dd-\{hh:mm}{\fs16\lang2057 \} | dd | all | }{\b\fs16\lang2057 never}{\fs16\lang2057 \tab // if vote closes never, organiser may send a closing command}{\fs18\lang2057 \par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 Invite=yes | }{\b\fs18\lang2057 no}{\fs18\lang2057 \tab \tab \tab \tab // send special invitation message to members of voting activity\par }\pard \qj\ri708\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 Remind=yyyy:mm:dd-\{hh:mm}{\fs16\lang2057 \} | dd | }{\b\fs16\lang2057 no}{\fs16\lang2057 \tab // dat or number of days before VoteCloses\par }{\fs18\lang2057 // The following entries specify the result calculations \par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs18\lang2057 RankingWinner=\tab \tab \tab \tab // only applicable for RankingChoice Model\par \tab \tab }{\b\fs18\lang2057 Alternative}{\fs18\lang2057  | \tab \tab // Majority is determined iteratively (Hare method)\par \tab \tab Sum | \tab \tab \tab // summarizes all ranks, may result in ambiguous results\par \tab \tab BinaryRankScore |  \tab // Each choice is compared to all other, victories are counted\par \tab \tab NetBinaryRankScore\tab // as BinaryRankScore, victories minus losses are counted\par Statistics=none | }{\b\fs18\lang2057 AllApplicable\tab \tab }{\fs18\lang2057 // more statistics can be only calculated for EvaluationChoice }{\b\fs18\lang2057 \par }{\fs18\lang2057 ExportVoteInputs=yes |}{\b\fs18\lang2057  no}{\fs18\lang2057 \tab \tab \tab // exports all votes to file of type  text/Web4Groups-VoteInputs\par }{\lang2057 \par Some voting models will need automatic checking of the user inputs. This can be handled for the web interface using JavaScript; an example for checking ranks can be found at: http://boris.qub.ac.uk/drn/prefer/vot1.html\par \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011256}Voting user interface mock-ups{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011256}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 Figures 7 and 8 below  show the sequence of messages in  a voting procedure. The example deals with  a discussion on flowers and gardens in which the wish to meet each other arises. John Smith raises the question when to meet next in Paradise, California (Figure 7) After some discussion Arthur Adams opens a vote on that topic. The voting board "Voting on: Next Meeting in Paradise" is displayed in the outline area of the discussion "Flowers and Gardens". Figure 8 shows the voting board itself. Its presentation area shows the voting form and additional explanatory text. In the voting board's outline view all the votes already submitted are displayed. Please note that this is only the case if intended by the voting board's organiser setting up the voting parameters. There will be no outline view at all, if it is decided not to show the votes to ordinary members.\par }\pard\plain \s18\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright