lowing  section rating is discussed in the context of group co-operation in CMC. As a specific consequence of rating, the role and the functions of participants might change depending on the ratings for their contributions.\par \par }\pard\plain \s2\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\i\f1\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505071}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505136}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505167}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505335}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373565153}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373651961}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373660854}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc381770872}\page {\*\bkmkstart _Toc382827287}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382828893}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc382896611}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011266}Introduction}{\ul\lang2057 {\*\bkmkend _Toc373505071}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505136}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505167}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505335}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373565153}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373651961}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373660854}{\*\bkmkend _Toc381770872}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382827287}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382828893}{\*\bkmkend _Toc382896611}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011266}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 In a way, this is a continuation of a paper about "social functions in virtual communities" (Alton-Scheidl, Diallo, Tscherteu 1996 available at http://www.soe.oeaw.ac.at/w4g/ project/social.html), where a system of flexible and context-sensitive role assignment was described. Like in "real life" roles should change according to the social settings in which a person participates. It is not self-evident that usage rights should be assigned without regard  to the social setting in which the usage takes place. CMC should  be a socially differentiated cultural space, like cultural spheres in \u8222\'e3normal life\ldblquote , and this would for example mean that a participant in  a discussion should have certain rights, different from somebody participating  in a market situation. Such a change from one social setting to another is described in Figure 1.1.\par \par }{\fs20\lang2057 {\pict