 three fruits may be awarded by directing fellows. Awarding fruits reduces the donor's account. Fruits of all kinds can be converted into each other. E.g. if a fellow from discussion A has obtained two shells, three acorns and one cactus, his account of fruits is six. Therefore he is allowed to give six acorns after becoming a directing fellow (because of rule 5) in discussion A. \par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 \par }{\i\lang2057 How to become a fellow?}{\lang2057 \par \par }\pard\plain \s23\qj\fi-1114\li1134\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1024\cgrid {\lang2057 Rule 3:\tab A newbie becomes a fellow by receiving any kind of fruit from a directing fellow.\par }\pard \s23\qj\fi-1100\li1120\widctlpar\adjustright {\lang2057 \par Rule 4:\tab A newbie becomes a fellow if he receives  three flowers from at least two different\tab persons.\par  \par }{\i\lang2057 How to become a directing fellow?}{\lang2057 \par \par Rule 5:\tab After obtaining three fruits of one kind, a fellow becomes a directing fellow in the respective discussion. Example: After obtaining  three acorns a fellow becomes directing fellow in discussion A (in figure 3). It is possible to be a directing fellow in different discussions.\par \par Rule 6:\tab After spending all his fruits he returns to being an ordinary fellow.\par \par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 These six basic rules are very simple, but nevertheless allow a great variety of possible behaviour and tactics by the players that need further discussion and additional rules, which are described in the following section.\par }{\fs28\lang2057 \par }\pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505077}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc373505142}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc384011271}Tuning the System{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505077}{\*\bkmkend _Toc373505142}{\*\bkmkend _Toc384011271}\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\i\lang2057 Getting and losing access}{\lang2057 \par It is quite easy to become a fellow: The rating mechanisms defined in rules 3 and 4 construct a kind of boundary that keeps unwanted people out. This coincides with what was stated above, that boundaries may increase the mutual benefit of members. It is a possible for a "gang" of three people to bypass rule 4 by awarding high ratings to each other. This may be avoided by special rules but such "gangs" may also be regarded to be  inspiring and innovating. If their influence on the discussion is considered destructive, they may be thrown out by a special rule, e.g.\par }\pard\plain \s23\qj\fi-1100\li1120\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1024\cgrid {\ul\lang2057 \par }{\lang2057 Rule 7a:\tab Two directing fellows are enough to throw a fellow out of the respective discussion. If there is only one directing fellow, that one has the right to ban fellows. Their fellowship is not influenced by being banned.\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 \par This is a rather authoritarian rule allowing fast reactions to unwanted people. It could be changed into a more democratic rule, like\par \par }\pard\plain \s23\qj\fi-1100\li1120\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1024\cgrid {\lang2057 Rule 7b:\tab The banning of people needs a voting procedure in which all members may take part. Simple majority is needed.\par }{\i\lang2057 \par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\i\lang2057 Directing discussions}{\lang2057 \par \par It is quite easy to become a fellow but not so easy to become a directing fellow. As pointed out above, there should be special rules preventing a directing fellow from keeping  that role for life. This may be acceptable in a traditional discipline but not in a context of very dynamic knowledge production. The rules already mentioned do not force directing fellows to spend their fruits. Therefore we have to define an additional one.\par \par }\pard\plain \s23\qj\fi-1100\li1120\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1024\cgrid {\lang2057 Rule 8\tab  A directing fellow must spend at least three fruits within one month. Recipients have to be ordinary fellows.\par \par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \lang1031\cgrid {\lang2057 This rule has two implications. First, it forces directing fellows to spend their fruits, and second it produces a new generation of directing fellows. Rule 8 is the key rule producing role rotation, as it is impossible to create a closed circuit of fruits among directing fellows only. One consequence of rule 8 might be that rotation only takes place among a limited number of persons (see figure 5).\par \par }\pard \qc\widctlpar\adjustright {\fs20\lang2057 {\pict\wmetafile8\picw7408\pich5715\picwgoal4200\pichgoal3240 010009000003270600000700580000000000050000000b0200000000050000000c02a200d2000400000004010d00040000002e011800040000000201010005000000090200000000050000000102ffffff00030000001e000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff0000000000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff00000000000007000000fc020000000000000000040000002d01000008000000fa0206000100000000000000040000002d01010007000000180454000d004d00060007000000fc020100000000000000040000002d01020007000000180457000f004b0003000700000018045a001200480000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff0100000000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff000000000000040000002d010000070000001804540095004d008e00040000002d010200070000001804570097004b008b000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff0100000000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff0000000000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff00000000000008000000fa020600060000007f7f7f00040000002d0103000b00000017084200e7ff26004a0056008f002e0006000b0000001708250046004200a90056008b002e0002000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff0100000000000a00000026060f000a00ffffffff00000000000035000000420105000000280000000800000008000000010001000000000008000000120b0000120b0000000000000000000000000000ffffff00aa00000055000000aa00000055000000aa00000055000000aa000000550000000000000000000